11. SQL Injection in GET vs POST
GET	POST
Visible in URL	Hidden in body
Easier to test	Slightly harder
Logged in history	Not logged
12. SQL Injection Prevention Techniques
12.1 Prepared Statements (Parameterized Queries)

Prevents query manipulation.

12.2 Input Validation

Allow only expected input

Reject special characters

12.3 Stored Procedures

Avoid dynamic SQL queries.

12.4 Web Application Firewall (WAF)

Blocks malicious payloads.

12.5 Least Privilege

Database user should have minimal permissions.

13. SQL Injection vs Other Attacks
SQL Injection	XSS
Database attack	Client-side attack
Affects backend	Affects users
Data extraction	Script execution
